he wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Information Technology Office: Assistant Director of Information Technology (Digital Transformation) (ITO) - ( 26002BB ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Information Technology Office Closing Date : 26/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Chief Information Officer (Digitalisation and A.I.), the appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Providing leadership for the planning, implementation and maintenance of the University’s Student Information Systems as well as related service and applications; Overseeing system integration, data quality and process optimisation to ensure efficient and effective information flow across academic schools and administrative offices; Collaborating with stakeholders to analyse needs, translate them into system requirements to meet the current and future needs of the University; Managing system upgrades, tenders, vendor relationships and project delivery to meet defined timelines and quality standards; Supervising an information system team to implement, develop, enhance and maintain ERP as well as other application systems of the University; and Performing any other duties as assigned. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree in Computer Science or Information Technology or related disciplines; Substantial knowledge and experience in Oracle/PeopleSoft development platform and technical infrastructure, mobile application development, AI implementation, web content management as well as hands-on experience in the implementation of student administration/ERP systems, admission/applicant website and student self-service portal, preferably with managerial experience in tertiary institutions; Solid and extensive experience in cloud platform administration and configuration is desirable; Profound leadership, independent and proactive with good analytical and problem-solving skills; Excellent vendor management, project management and conflict management skills; and Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, and proficient in both English & Chinese. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26002BC": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Information Technology (Management Information Systems) (ITO) (26002BC)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Director of Information Technology (Management Information Systems) (ITO) (26002BC) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Director of Information Technology (Management Information Systems) (ITO) (26002BC) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Information Technology Office: Assistant Director of Information Technology (Management Information Systems) (ITO) - ( 26002BC ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Information Technology Office Closing Date : 26/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Chief Information Officer, the appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Leading the Management Information Systems team to plan, develop, enhance, and maintain management information systems for the University, such as Human Resources Management System, Financial Management Systems, Facility Management System, Customer Relationship Management System, Access Control System, and Information Enquiry and Broadcasting Systems; Developing, reviewing, and implementing policies and guidelines to provide quality application system services; Managing internal resources and external resources, such as vendors, to implement application system projects; Providing professional advice and support to users on application system implementation; Providing executive support to committees and working groups; and Performing any other duties as assigned. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or a related discipline; Substantial knowledge and experience in supporting Oracle e-Business Suite development platform and technical infrastructure, as well as hands-on experience in the implementation ERP systems and online self-services, preferably with managerial experience in tertiary institutions; Solid and extensive experience in web/application/database server administration and configuration is desirable; Profound leadership, independent and proactive with good analytical and problem-solving skills; and Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, and proficient in both English & Chinese Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26002BD": {
      "title": "Senior Information Technology Manager (Digital Transformation) (ITO) (26002BD)",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Information Technology Manager (Digital Transformation) (ITO)  (26002BD) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Information Technology Manager (Digital Transformation) (ITO)  (26002BD) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Information Technology Office: Senior Information Technology Manager (Digital Transformation) (ITO) - ( 26002BD ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Information Technology Office Closing Date : 26/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Chief Information Officer (Digitalisation and A.I.), the appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Providing leadership for the planning, implementation and maintenance of the University’s AI Platforms and related services and applications; Overseeing AI system development, integration, data security and process automation to ensure efficient and effective operations across academic schools and administrative offices; Collaborating with stakeholders to analyse needs and translate them into system requirements that meet the current and future needs of the University; Organising AI training sessions and promoting AI tools/solutions to students, administrative staff, academic staff and researcher to support AI in teaching and learning, research, administrative operations; Supervising an information system team to develop, enhance and maintain University’s AI platforms, AI tools, AI-enabled applications and automation solutions; and Performing any other duties as assigned. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree in Computer Science or Information Technology or related disciplines; Substantial knowledge and experience in designing, developing, integrating and supporting AI-enabled applications and automation solutions to enhance the new Student Administration System and other University operations and services; Experience in integrating AI platforms/tools, application APIs and internal/external systems to automate processes, improve service efficiency and support University operational needs; Hands-on experience in the implementing AI workflows, AI agent systems, admission/applicant websites and student self-service portal, preferably with managerial experience in tertiary institutions; Solid and extensive experience in cloud platform administration and configuration is desirable; Ability to evaluate and adopt emerging AI, agentic, cloud and application technologies to meet University initiatives; Proven ability to collaborate with other IT/IS teams, vendors, systems implementers and user departments; and Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, and proficient in both English & Chinese. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260027I": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager / Library Officer (Library Systems and Technology) (LIB) (260027I)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Manager / Library Officer (Library Systems and Technology) (LIB) (260027I) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Manager / Library Officer (Library Systems and Technology) (LIB) (260027I) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Library : Assistant Manager / Library Officer (Library Systems and Technology) (LIB) - ( 260027I ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Library Closing Date : 22/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Assisting in overseeing daily operations of the Library Systems and Technology Section; Assisting in planning, coordinating, and managing activities related to library systems and technology; Assisting in formulating policies and procedures related to library systems and technology; Assisting in administering the Alma integrated library system, link resolver, Primo discovery portal, and other digital systems of the Library; Assisting in developing and maintaining the Library’s application programmes and database systems; Serving on committees and task forces as appropriate; and Performing any other duties as assigned by the University Librarian or his/her nominee. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree; At least 2 years’ relevant post-qualification experience (for Assistant Manager); Substantial relevant post-qualification experience in library systems in an academic library is advantageous; Hands-on experience in managing software, hardware running various operating systems, and networking is advantageous; Working knowledge of HTML, XML, Java, JavaScript, CSS, PHP, MySQL, etc. is preferred; and Good interpersonal and communication skills in both English and Chinese. Applicants with less relevant experience may be considered for appointment as Library Officer. Candidates with a professional library qualification (e.g., AALIA, ALA, MCLIP, MLIS or equivalent) may be appointed as Assistant Librarian II, commensurate with work experience. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in October 2025 - September 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=260027D": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor (Information Systems) (B&A) (260027D)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor (Information Systems) (B&A) (260027D) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor (Information Systems) (B&A) (260027D) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . About the Lee Shau Kee School of Business & Administration The Lee Shau Kee School of Business and Administration at HKMU is one of the largest business schools in Hong Kong, serving over 4,500 students across a comprehensive range of undergraduate, postgraduate, and doctoral programs, and is home to over 150 faculty members across 3 departments. The school is highly regarded for its professional recognition, with many programs holding accreditations or exemptions from major international accounting and business bodies. It strongly emphasizes career readiness by providing internships and global immersion opportunities, while also driving top-quality regionally relevant research through well-resourced infrastructures such as the Institute of International Business and Governance (IIBG). The School is ranked in the global top 150 for Hospitality and Leisure Management in the QS World University Subject Rankings 2026. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Lee Shau Kee School of Business and Administration : Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor (Information Systems) (B&A) - ( 260027D ) Job : Full-time Academic School/Unit : Lee Shau Kee School of Business and Administration Closing Date : 10/Dec/2026, 7:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Research Excellence: Maintaining an active, high-impact research pipeline. Assistant Professors must demonstrate strong potential to publish in top-tier journals, while Associate Professors and Professors must possess an established, internationally recognized track record of elite publications (e.g., MIS Quarterly, Information Systems Research, and other UTD 24, FT50, ABS 4* journals), as well as a proven ability to secure research funding; Instruction & Curriculum: Teaching core and elective Information Systems and related courses at the undergraduate, MBA, and PhD levels. Developing and delivering modern curricula around business AI applications, data analytics, and digital business transformation; and Institutional Leadership: (For Associate Professors and Professors) Providing mentorship to junior faculty and doctoral students, spearheading departmental initiatives, and maintaining visible engagement within the global and local professional and academic bodies. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: Education: A Ph.D. or equivalent doctoral degree in Information Systems, Business Analytics, Quantitative Marketing, or a closely related business discipline must be completed prior to the appointment start date; Assistant Professors: High potential for publishing in premier IS journals and evidence of teaching effectiveness; Associate Professors and Professors: A proven record of continuous top-tier publication, teaching excellence, academic leadership, and national/ international visibility; Highly desired expertise in AI-driven business strategy, algorithmic governance, responsible AI, or human-AI collaboration; Demonstrated ability to bridge technical fields (e.g., Python, machine learning models) with strategic business and management principles; and Experience in securing external research funding or building industry partnerships is preferred. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidate. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System and upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae; Job-market paper; Research statement (including publication record and pipeline); and At least three referee letters. Please note that the University’s eRecruitment System allows a maximum of three (3) file attachments per application. Candidates are therefore requested to consolidate the required application materials into no more than three PDF files prior to submission. Application & ICIS 2026 Interview Process To be fully considered, applications must be submitted through our portal no later than 10 December 2026. Important ICIS Note: Search committee representatives will be present at the International Conference on Information Systems (ICIS). Preliminary interviews will be conducted onsite using the AIS Career Connect platform or other means. Candidates attending ICIS who wish to schedule an interview slot are highly encouraged to submit their initial application package early. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600279": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer / Lecturer (Clinical) (N&HS)",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Lecturer / Lecturer (Clinical) (N&HS) (2600279) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Lecturer / Lecturer (Clinical) (N&HS) (2600279) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences : Senior Lecturer / Lecturer (Clinical) (N&HS) - ( 2600279 ) Job : Full-time Academic School/Unit : School of Nursing and Health Sciences Closing Date : 22/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: undertaking course planning and development; undertaking course coordination, clinical assessments and mentoring, and classroom teaching in Nursing and related disciplines/areas; undertaking/engaging in scholarly activities/academic research and participating in School/University activities and administration; and performing any duties assigned by the Dean. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: a Master’s degree in Nursing or a related health discipline; professional registration/licensure with relevant Boards/Councils as appropriate; relevant teaching experience with at least 5 years’ of professional experience, preferably in the areas of Adult and Child Nursing or other Clinical Nursing Specialties; track record in relevant research areas where appropriate, and a good command of English and Chinese. The level of appointment depends on the candidate’s academic background, experience and competence in academic leadership, teaching, research, scholarly publications, etc. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. “Accommodation Programme for Overseas Young Teaching Staff” sponsored by the “Katie Shu Sui Pui Charitable Trust” Overseas candidates who are successfully appointed by the University and below age 50 will be eligible to apply for the “Accommodation Programme for Overseas Young Teaching Staff” sponsored by the “Katie Shu Sui Pui Charitable Trust”. This programme offers the opportunity to reside in assigned accommodation free of charge for a period of up to six months, subject to terms and conditions. To Apply Please submit your application via the University’s eRecruitment System. The University will review your application and contact you should there be a suitable vacancy. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in August 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
