    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26002BN": {
      "title": "Associate Director (LiPACE) (26002BN)",
      "description": "Job Description - Associate Director (LiPACE) (26002BN) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Associate Director (LiPACE) (26002BN) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . Li Ka Shing School of Professional & Continuing Education (LiPACE) As one of the eight schools of HKMU, LiPACE has a strong track record of serving diverse learner groups in Hong Kong. Established in 1992 as the Centre for Continuing and Community Education, the institution was elevated to an Institute in 2000 and officially named LiPACE. In January 2020, the University Council approved LiPACE’s normalization as a School, marking a major milestone in its development. As the designated professional and continuing education arm of the University, LiPACE is committed to providing high-quality learning opportunities with a primary focus on Vocational and Professional Education and Training (VPET). This distinctive role differentiates it from the other schools of the University, which primarily offer bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral programmes through full-time and distance learning modes. LiPACE’s academic remit and community engagement activities are organized around four key programme areas: (1) Further Education, (2) Access Programmes, (3) Professional and Continuing Education and Corporate Training, and (4) Adult Education. Beyond these core areas, LiPACE actively promotes non-formal learning in the community through targeted projects. In fulfilling the University’s founding mission of “education for all,” LiPACE complements the broader academic offerings by covering a wide range of disciplines and study levels, while serving learners of diverse ages, nationalities, and occupations. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position(s) in the LiPACE : Associate Director (LiPACE) - ( 26002BN ) Job : Full-time Academic School/Unit : Li Ka Shing School of Professional and Continuing Education Closing Date : 31/Oct/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Dean of Li Ka Shing School of Professional & Continuing Education, the appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Assisting the Dean in the overall management of the School; Providing academic leadership and guidance for the planning, development, delivery and quality assurance of programmes and courses; Supervising administrative units and academic divisions; Assisting the Dean to implement collaborations and projects with external partners; Engaging in scholarly and professional activities; Participating in School/University activities and administration; and Performing any other duties as assigned by the Dean (LiPACE). Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A higher degree (preferably an earned doctorate) and professional qualification in relevant areas; Substantial teaching/management experience in tertiary/post-secondary/continuing and professional education and professional experience in the related subject; Having strong ability to build rapport with a broad spectrum of stakeholders; Active involvement in scholarly, professional and community activities is required; and Excellent interpersonal skills and be proficient in English & Chinese languages (preferably including Putonghua). Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.  For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26002BI": {
