    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26002DK": {
      "title": "Postdoc (N&HS) (26002DK)",
      "description": "Job Description - Postdoc (N&HS) (26002DK) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Postdoc (N&HS) (26002DK) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences : Postdoc (N&HS) - ( 26002DK ) Job : Full-time R&D School/Unit : School of Nursing and Health Sciences Closing Date : 06/Nov/2026, 7:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Design and conduct research in chemical biology, with particular emphasis on protein biochemistry, protein immobilisation, bioconjugation and enzyme-based biosensor development; Develop and optimise protein immobilisation and bioconjugation strategies, including surface functionalisation, site-specific conjugation and linker design, to preserve protein activity, accessibility, orientation and stability; Investigate the effects of immobilisation chemistry, conjugation methods and surface properties on protein function, enzyme activity and biosensor performance; Design and optimise enzyme-based biochemical assays, including characterisation of enzyme kinetics, reaction mechanisms and assay performance; Develop and validate biochemical detection platforms, evaluating their sensitivity, specificity, reproducibility, stability and robustness; Analyse and interpret experimental data, troubleshoot technical challenges and collaborate with an interdisciplinary research team; Prepare manuscripts, research reports and presentations, and contribute to research funding applications; and Support research student training, maintain accurate laboratory records and coordinate day-to-day research activities. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: Hold a PhD in Chemical Biology, Biochemistry, Protein Chemistry, Biotechnology, Biomedical Engineering or a closely related discipline, awarded within the past three years. PhD candidates with a strong relevant research background who expect to obtain their degree within the next six months will also be considered; Have hands-on research experience in chemical biology, particularly protein immobilisation, bioconjugation, protein modification or surface functionalisation; Possess practical knowledge of protein biochemistry and experience in developing or optimising biochemical assays involving enzymes or other functional proteins; Demonstrate an understanding of the chemical principles underlying protein–surface interactions, conjugation chemistry and the effects of chemical modification on protein structure and function; Demonstrate the ability to independently design experiments, develop and optimise laboratory protocols, troubleshoot experimental problems and critically interpret quantitative data; Have good scientific writing and communication skills in English and the ability to work effectively within an interdisciplinary research team; and Demonstrate research achievements appropriate to their career stage. Experience in site-specific protein conjugation, enzyme kinetics, biosensor development or quantitative data analysis using Python, R, MATLAB or equivalent software would be an advantage. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary and an end-of-contract gratuity will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. Duration: 24-months To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref. 2600245) posted in Oct 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
