      "title": "Laboratory Technician (LiPACE) (26002DH)",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Technician (LiPACE)  (26002DH) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Technician (LiPACE)  (26002DH) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk. Li Ka Shing School of Professional & Continuing Education (LiPACE) As one of the eight schools of HKMU, LiPACE has a strong track record of serving diverse learner groups in Hong Kong. Established in 1992 as the Centre for Continuing and Community Education, the institution was elevated to an Institute in 2000 and officially named LiPACE. In January 2020, the University Council approved LiPACE’s normalization as a School, marking a major milestone in its development. As the designated professional and continuing education arm of the University, LiPACE is committed to providing high-quality learning opportunities with a primary focus on Vocational and Professional Education and Training (VPET). This distinctive role differentiates it from the other schools of the University, which primarily offer bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral programmes through full-time and distance learning modes. LiPACE’s academic remit and community engagement activities are organized around four key programme areas: (1) Further Education, (2) Access Programmes, (3) Professional and Continuing Education and Corporate Training, and (4) Adult Education. Beyond these core areas, LiPACE actively promotes non-formal learning in the community through targeted projects. In fulfilling the University’s founding mission of “education for all,” LiPACE complements the broader academic offerings by covering a wide range of disciplines and study levels, while serving learners of diverse ages, nationalities, and occupations. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the LiPACE: Laboratory Technician (LiPACE) - ( 26002DH ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Li Ka Shing School of Professional and Continuing Education Closing Date : 04/Nov/2026, 7:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Overseeing daily laboratory operations, including inventory management and equipment maintenance; Providing technical support for the operation of laboratories in projects, workshops, and course delivery; Managing laboratory setups and equipment acquisition; Demonstrating experiments and training students and users on equipment; Ensuring laboratory safety and security; and Performing any other duties as assigned by supervisors. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A Higher Diploma or above, preferably a Bachelor’s degree, in Science or Technology, or Engineering disciplines; Preference for candidates with work experience in teaching laboratories of engineering in postsecondary institutions; Experience in operating and maintaining Civil Engineering laboratory instruments is an advantage; Being detail oriented, hardworking, responsible, able to meet deadlines, and capable of working independently; Strong interpersonal and management skills; and Proficiency in both English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua. Candidates may be invited to attend a written test. T erms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26002CX": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (S&T) (26002CX)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor (S&T) (26002CX) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor (S&T) (26002CX) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position(s) in the School of Science and Technology : Assistant Professor (S&T) - ( 26002CX ) Job : Full-time Academic School/Unit : School of Science and Technology Closing Date : 03/Nov/2026, 7:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Undertaking course planning, development, coordination and delivery (including classroom, laboratory, and project-based teaching) in areas related to environmental science, green technology, or equivalent; Participating in programme development, quality assurance, and/or accreditation exercise; Performing scholarly activities, producing high-quality publications, and pursuing external research funding in related discipline(s); Leading and promoting research collaborations with academic and industrial partners; Supervising undergraduate and postgraduate research project(s); Supporting student development activities, including mentoring, competitions, and experiential learning; Undertaking / participating in School and University-wide activities and administration; and Performing any other duties as assigned by supervisors. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A doctoral degree in Environmental Science, Green Technology, Cosmetic Science or a related discipline; Relevant experience in the tertiary education sector; Competence in teaching / professional experience including programme development and course administration; Strong communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction; A distinguished record of peer-reviewed publications in reputable journals and leading conferences; Substantial industrial or professional experience in environmental science, green technology, Cosmetic Science or a related sector; A track record of applied research, technology transfer, consulting, or co-developed industry projects are preferred; and A record of securing competitive research funding will be an advantage. Applicants who have less extensive experience and/or do not fully meet the requirements for appointment as Assistant Professor may be considered for appointment as Senior Lecturer. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. “Accommodation Programme for Overseas Young Teaching Staff” sponsored by the “Katie Shu Sui Pui Charitable Trust” Overseas candidates who are successfully appointed by the University and below age 50 will be eligible to apply for the “Accommodation Programme for Overseas Young Teaching Staff” sponsored by the “Katie Shu Sui Pui Charitable Trust”.  This programme offers the opportunity to reside in assigned accommodation free of charge for a period of up to six months, subject to terms and conditions. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.  For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26002D1": {
      "title": "Officer (Editorial and Publications) (A&SS) (26002D1)",
      "description": "Job Description - Officer (Editorial and Publications) (A&SS) (26002D1) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Officer (Editorial and Publications) (A&SS) (26002D1) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Wu Jieh Yee School of Arts and Social Sciences : Officer (Editorial and Publications) (A&SS) - ( 26002D1 ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Wu Jieh Yee School of Arts and Social Sciences Closing Date : 02/Nov/2026, 7:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following for the Tin Ka Ping Centre of Chinese Culture: Conducting preliminary and background research to support the Tin Ka Ping Centre of Chinese Culture (the Centre)’s publications, reports and editorial projects; Managing editorial workflow, including tracking timelines, collecting drafts, and maintaining version control; Editing, proofreading, fact-checking copy for accuracy, style and consistency; Preparing and formatting documents for print and digital publication; Arranging and coordinating interviews and related logistics; Maintaining publication records, archives and content management entries; Providing support to the Centre in office administration, coordination and liaison with internal and external parties at various levels; Providing general support to the daily operations including programmes, projects and activities carried out by the Centre; and Performing any other duties as assigned by the Centre Director or his/her nominee(s). Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree or above, a degree in English, Chinese Language, Literature, Translation, Journalism, Community, Linguistics, History or a related field is preferred; Strong organisational and planning skills, with good interpersonal and communication abilities; Proficient in MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and competent with editing tools; Be self-motivated and meticulous, and be able to meet deadlines and work independently ; and Experience in editing or publishing would be an advantage. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
