rmation about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Wu Jieh Yee School of Arts and Social Sciences : Officer (Ina Ho Cantonese Opera Research Centre) (A&SS) - ( 26002D0 ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Wu Jieh Yee School of Arts and Social Sciences Closing Date : 02/Nov/2026, 7:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will assist the operation of Cantonese Opera Research Centre in various aspects. The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Providing support in the organisation of all events; Assisting in the promotion of all events within the Centre, including designing promotional materials; Facilitating effective communication with different stakeholders; Supporting the Centre in managing the budget and tracking expenses; Providing support to the research team, coordination and liaison with internal and external parties at various levels; Organising academic conference(s) and seminar(s); and Performing other duties as assigned. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A recognised degree in language, literature, translation, theatre, opera music or a related discipline; Preferably have experience in data analyses and research works; Strong organisational and planning skills, good interpersonal and communication skills, and competent at computer skills (MS Office using Word, Excel, PowerPoint etc.) as well as editing skills; Good command of English and Chinese (Cantonese and Putonghua); and Detail-oriented, hardworking, responsible, and able to meet deadlines and work independently. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental 